  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run; branch jgstern-agent/fix/kabaf, commit 1f4c88c755, NOT pushed; integrator closes).\n\nPREMISE RE-VERIFIED at 62602239c6. The three sites moved (now ci.yml:650, :706, :1049) but are unchanged. Executing the extracted validate blocks against fabricated manifests: root-level-only selection of 2 tests printed \"manifest lists 0<newline>0 test files\" (grep -c prints 0 AND exits 1, so `|| echo 0` doubles it); a manifest of 2 changed sources + 3 selected tests printed 4 (the prefix also matches CHANGED_SOURCE_FILES lines and misses the root-level test). So the count was wrong in BOTH directions, not only 0.\n\nWHICH FILE RUNS PER PR: .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml (status context ci/woodpecker/pr/woodpecker). .github/workflows/ci.yml does NOT run: GitHub Actions is disabled under Woodpecker (scripts/ci-debug GitHub arm; WI-bavak) -- a recorded claim, not re-checked live by me (no API call made). The live Woodpecker pytest step counts the SELECTED_TESTS section with wc -w and had no prefix count; its \"=== pytest (N selected files\" line is correct for the root-level shape (now pinned). So the blast radius of this row is a diagnostic in a dormant file.\n\nFIX: each site counts the SELECTED_TESTS section (the section the run step reads) with `grep -c . || true`; the validated banner reuses TEST_COUNT. .woodpecker/ untouched.\n\nTESTS: new tests/test_ci_github_manifest_count.py (19 cases: both validate blocks executed under bash -e and -eo pipefail with a replaced PATH, root-level / mixed / empty manifests, plus a sweep of every .github/workflows/*.yml and .woodpecker/*.yml for a prefix-keyed grep -c); one control added to tests/test_ci_pytest_selection_gate.py for the live Woodpecker count. Red before the fix: 10 failed / 9 passed. Mutation (retry site reverted + Woodpecker count switched to the prefix form): exactly the 7 predicted tests red, pytest-job cases stayed green. Final targeted smart-test on the commit: 2071 passed, 0 failed (122 files). No package source changed, so the scoped coverage gate had nothing to enforce.\n\nNOT CHANGED: scripts/smart-test:1405 has the same `grep -c . || echo 0` double-zero shape, but it is reachable with 0 only when every package in a version-only change has no test files (htrac-frontend has no Python source), so not filed."  # 8a56
